n the source answer bank.","model":"Induction introduces the employee to colleagues and reporting relationships.","alternatives":[]}],"choiceBank":[{"model":"Induction helps the new employee understand the duties of the job.","alternatives":[]},{"model":"Induction explains the organisation’s rules and safety procedures.","alternatives":[]},{"model":"Induction introduces the employee to colleagues and reporting relationships.","alternatives":[]},{"model":"Induction can reduce uncertainty and help the employee settle into the organisation.","alternatives":[]}]},"prompt":"State THREE benefits of an induction programme for a new employee.","expectedAnswer":"Induction helps the new employee understand the duties of the job.\nInduction explains the organisation’s rules and safety procedures.\nInduction introduces the employee to colleagues and reporting relationships.","rubricVersion":"oa-source-rubric-v2-2026-10-26"},{"id":"OA-ORIGINAL-02-01-Q4::q4-c","maxMarks":9,"kind":"structured","sourceFormat":"oa-original-paper2","sourcePaperId":"OA-ORIGINAL-02-01","sourceQuestion":4,"sourcePartId":"q4-c","sourceVersion":"oa-paper2-original-2026-10-26-v1","sourceMarking":{"criteria":[{"id":"q4-c-c1","marks":1,"rule":"Employee: Ms Mia Lewis","kind":"field","label":"Employee","expected":"Ms Mia Lewis","alternatives":["Mia Lewis"],"labelAliases":[],"model":"Employee: Ms Mia Lewis"},{"id":"q4-c-c2","marks":1,"rule":"Post: Records clerk","kind":"field","label":"Post","expected":"Records clerk","alternatives":[],"labelAliases":[],"model":"Post: Records clerk"},{"id":"q4-c-c3","marks":1,"rule":"Supervisor: Mr Andre Smith, office manager","kind":"field","label":"Supervisor","expected":"Mr Andre Smith, office manager","alternatives":["Andre Smith, office manager"],"labelAliases":[],"model":"Supervisor: Mr Andre Smith, office manager"},{"id":"q4-c-c4","marks":1,"rule":"Workplace: Kingston office","kind":"field","label":"Workplace","expected":"Kingston office","alternatives":[],"labelAliases":[],"model":"Workplace: Kingston office"},{"id":"q4-c-c5","marks":1,"rule":"Start date: 5 July 2027","kind":"field","label":"Start date","expected":"5 July 2027","alternatives":[],"labelAliases":[],"model":"Start date: 5 July 2027"},{"id":"q4-c-c6","marks":1,"rule":"Working hours: Monday to Friday, 8:30 a.m.–4:30 p.m.","kind":"field","label":"Working hours","expected":"Monday to Friday, 8:30 a.m.–4:30 p.m.","alternatives":["Monday–Friday 08:30–16:30","Monday to Friday 8:30 am to 4:30 pm"],"labelAliases":[],"model":"Working hours: Monday to Friday, 8:30 a.m.–4:30 p.m."},{"id":"q4-c-c7","marks":1,"rule":"Monthly salary: J$95,000","kind":"numeric","label":"Monthly salary","expected":95000,"unit":"J$","tolerance":0.005,"labelAliases":[],"model":"Monthly salary: J$95,000"},{"id":"q4-c-c8","marks":1,"rule":"Probation: Three months","kind":"field","label":"Probation","expected":"Three months","alternatives":["3 months"],"labelAliases":[],"model":"Probation: Three months"},{"id":"q4-c-c9","marks":1,"rule":"Acceptance deadline: 25 June 2027","kind":"field","label":"Acceptance deadline","expected":"25 June 2027","alternatives":[],"labelAliases":[],"model":"Acceptance deadline: 25 June 2027"}]},"prompt":"Prepare the main information for the appointment letter. Use these NINE labels: Employee; Post; Supervisor; Workplace; Start date; Working hours; Monthly salary; Probation; Acceptance deadline.","expectedAnswer":"Employee: Ms Mia Lewis\nPost: Records clerk\nSupervisor: Mr Andre Smith, office manager\nWorkplace: Kingston office\nStart date: 5 July 2027\nWorking hours: Monday to Friday, 8:30 a.m.–4:30 p.m.\nMonthly salary: J$95,000\nProbation: Three months\nAcceptance deadline: 25 June 2027","rubricVersion":"oa-source-rubric-v2-2026-10-26"},{"id":"OA-ORIGINAL-02-01-Q5::q5-a","maxMarks":3,"kind":"structured","sourceFormat":"oa-original-paper2","sourcePaperId":"OA-ORIGINAL-02-01","sourceQuestion":5,"sourcePartId":"q5-a","sourceVersion":"oa-paper2-original-2026-10-26-v1","sourceMarking":{"criteria":[{"id":"q5-a-c1","marks":1,"rule":"One distinct correct point (1 of 3); accept the alternatives in the source answer bank.","model":"A purchase requisition asks the purchasing department to obtain goods needed by another department.","alternatives":[]},{"id":"q5-a-c2","marks":1,"rule":"One distinct correct point (2 of 3); accept the alternatives in the source answer bank.","model":"A purchase order tells a supplier which goods the business agrees to purchase.","alternatives":[]},{"id":"q5-a-c3","marks":1,"rule":"One distinct correct point (3 of 3); accept the alternatives in the source answer bank.","model":"A supplier invoice requests payment for goods supplied and shows the amount due.","alternatives":[]}],"choiceBank":[{"model":"A purchase requisition asks the purchasing department to obtain goods needed by another department.","alternatives":[]},{"model":"A purchase order tells a supplier which goods the business agrees to purchase.","alternatives":[]},{"model":"A supplier invoice requests payment for goods supplied and shows the amount due.","alternatives":[]}]},"prompt":"State the purpose of a purchase requisition, a purchase order and a supplier invoice.","expectedAnswer":"A purchase requisition asks the purchasing department to obtain goods needed by another department.\nA purchase order tells a supplier which goods the business agrees to purchase.\nA supplier invoice requests payment for goods supplied and shows the amount due.","rubricVersion":"oa-source-rubric-v2-2026-10-26"},{"id":"OA-ORIGINAL-02-01-Q5::q5-b","maxMarks":3,"kind":"structured","sourceFormat":"oa-original-paper2","sourcePaperId":"OA-ORIGINAL-02-01","sourceQuestion":5,"sourcePartId":"q5-b","sourceVersion":"oa-paper2-original-2026-10-26-v1","sourceMarking":{"criteria":[{"id":"q5-b-c1","marks":1,"rule":"One distinct correct point (1 of 3); accept the alternatives in the source answer bank.","model":"An authorised officer should approve a payment before it is released.","alternatives":[]},{"id":"q5-b-c2","marks":1,"rule":"One distinct correct point (2 of 3); accept the alternatives in the source answer bank.","model":"The purchase order, goods received note and supplier invoice should agree before payment.","alternatives":[]},{"id":"q5-b-c3","marks":1,"rule":"One distinct correct point (3 of 3); accept the alternatives in the source answer bank.","model":"Different people should authorise a payment and record the transaction.","alternatives":[]}],"choiceBank":[{"model":"An authorised officer should approve a payment before it is released.","alternatives":[]},{"model":"The purchase order, goods received note and supplier invoice should agree before payment.","alternatives":[]},{"model":"Different people should authorise a payment and record the transaction.","alternatives":[]},{"model":"Paid invoices should be marked as paid to prevent duplicate payments.","alternatives":[]},{"model":"The payee and bank details should be checked against an approved supplier record.","alternatives":[]}]},"prompt":"Outline THREE controls that help prevent incorrect or unauthorised payments.","expectedAnswer":"An authorised officer should approve a payment before it is released.\nThe purchase order, goods received note and supplier invoice should agree before payment.\nDifferent people should authorise a payment and record the transaction.","rubricVersion":"oa-source-rubric-v2-2026-10-26"},{"id":"OA-ORIGINAL-02-01-Q5::q5-c","maxMarks":9,"kind":"structured","sourceFormat":"oa-original-paper2","sourcePaperId":"OA-ORIGINAL-02-01","sourceQuestion":5,"sourcePartId":"q5-c","sourceVersion":"oa-paper2-original-2026-10-26-v1","sourceMarking":{"criteria":[{"id":"q5-c-c1","marks":1,"rule":"Ordinary pay: J$4,800","kind":"numeric","label":"Ordinary pay","expected":4800,"unit":"J$","tolerance":0.005,"labelAliases":["Basic pay"],"model":"Ordinary pay: J$4,800"},{"id":"q5-c-c2","marks":1,"rule":"Overtime hourly rate: J$180","kind":"numeric","label":"Overtime hourly rate","expected":180,"unit":"J$","tolerance":0.005,"labelAliases":[],"model":"Overtime hourly rate: J$180"},{"id":"q5-c-c3","marks":1,"rule":"Overtime pay: J$900","kind":"numeric","label":"Overtime pay","expected":900,"unit":"J$","tolerance":0.005,"labelAliases":[],"model":"Overtime pay: J$900"},{"id":"q5-c-c4","marks":1,"rule":"Gross pay: J$5,700","kind":"numeric","label":"Gross pay","expected":5700,"unit":"J$","tolerance":0.005,"labelAliases":[],"model":"Gross pay: J$5,700"},{"id":"q5-c-c5","marks":1,"rule":"Income tax: J$420","kind":"numeric","label":"Income tax","expected":420,"unit":"J$","tolerance":0.005,"labelAliases":[],"model":"Income tax: J$420"},{"id":"q5-c-c6","marks":1,"rule":"Pension: J$250","kind":"numeric","label":"Pension","expected":250,"unit":"J$","tolerance":0.005,"labelAliases":[],"model":"Pension: J$250"},{"id":"q5-c-c7","marks":1,"rule":"Other deductions: J$230","kind":"numeric","label":"Other deductions","expected":230,"unit":"J$","tolerance":0.005,"labelAliases":[],"model":"Other deductions: J$230"},{"id":"q5-c-c8","marks":1,"rule":"Total deductions: J$900","kind":"numeric","label":"Total deductions","expected":900,"unit":"J$","tolerance":0.005,"labelAliases":[],"model":"Total deductions: J$900"},{"id":"q5-c-c9","marks":1,"rule":"Net pay: J$4,800","kind":"numeric","label":"Net pay","expected":4800,"unit":"J$","tolerance":0.005,"labelAliases":[],"model":"Net pay: J$4,800"}]},"prompt":"Complete the payroll calculation. Use these NINE labels: Ordinary pay; Overtime hourly rate; Overtime pay; Gross pay; Income tax; Pension; Other deductions; Total deductions; Net pay. Show your working.","expectedAnswer":"Ordinary pay: J$4,800\nOvertime hourly rate: J$180\nOvertime pay: J$900\nGross pay: J$5,700\nIncome tax: J$420\nPension: J$250\nOther deductions: J$230\nTotal deductions: J$900\nNet pay: J$4,800","rubricVersion":"oa-source-rubric-v2-2026-10-26"},{"id":"OA-ORIGINAL-02-01-Q6::q6-a","maxMarks":3,"kind":"structured","sourceFormat":"oa-original-paper2","sou